  <ferc:DisclosureOfImportantDisclosuresRegardingTheFinancialStatementsTextBlock id="f-1" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;NOTE 1 &#8211; Summary of Significant Accounting Policies&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;Organization and Nature of Operations&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt;text-indent:18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Ameren Services Company (the Company) is a wholly owned subsidiary of Ameren Corporation (Ameren), a public utility holding company under the Public Utility Holding Company Act of 2005 (PUHCA 2005). The Company was authorized to conduct business as a service company for Ameren and its various subsidiaries by order of the Securities and Exchange Commission (SEC) dated December 30, 1997, issued under the Public Utility Holding Company Act of 1935. The Company is organized along functional lines to accomplish its purpose of providing management, administrative, and technical services. These services are priced so that the Company operates on a break-even basis.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt;text-indent:18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The Company maintains its accounts in accordance with PUHCA 2005, as administered by the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission (FERC), and has adopted a system of accounts consistent with that prescribed by the FERC. The accompanying financial statements have been prepared in accordance with the accounting requirements of the FERC as set forth in the Uniform System of Accounts (USOA) and accounting releases, which require certain differences from accounting principles generally accepted in the United States (GAAP).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;Property, Plant, and Equipment &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt;text-indent:18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The cost of additions to and betterments of units of property, plant, and equipment are capitalized. The cost includes labor, material, applicable taxes and overheads. Maintenance expenditures are expensed as incurred. When units of depreciable property are retired, the original cost, less salvage value, are charged to accumulated depreciation. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;Depreciation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt;text-indent:18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Depreciation is provided over the estimated lives of the various classes of depreciable property by applying composite rates on a straight-line basis to the cost basis of such property. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;Cash and Cash Equivalents&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt;text-indent:18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Cash and cash equivalents include short-term, highly liquid investments purchased with an original maturity of three months or less.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;Income Taxes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt;text-indent:18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Ameren and its subsidiaries file a consolidated federal tax return. Deferred tax assets and liabilities are recognized for transactions that have been treated differently for financial reporting and income tax return purposes. These deferred tax assets and liabilities are based on statutory tax rates. The Company&#8217;s expenses are billed to the other subsidiaries of Ameren, and taxes are computed on those entities.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;Use of Estimates&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt;text-indent:18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The preparation of financial statements in conformity with GAAP requires management to make certain estimates and assumptions. Such estimates and assumptions affect reported amounts of assets and liabilities, the disclosure of contingent assets and liabilities at the dates of the financial statements, and the reported amounts of revenues and expenses during the reported periods. Actual results could differ from those estimates.&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;NOTE 2 &#8211; Common Stock&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt;text-indent:18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The Company is authorized to issue 30,000 shares of common stock at a par value of one cent ($0.01) per share. Ameren holds all of the Company&#8217;s common stock. At December 31, 2025 and 2024, there were 1,000 shares outstanding.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;NOTE 3 &#8211; Financing Arrangements&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt;text-indent:18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Ameren has money pool agreements among its subsidiaries to coordinate and provide for certain short-term cash and working capital requirements. The money pools are administered by the Company (see Note 4).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;NOTE 4 &#8211; Related Party Transactions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt;text-indent:18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The Company has transactions in the normal course of business with other Ameren subsidiaries. These transactions are primarily comprised of services received or rendered. Affiliate receivables were approximately $145 million and $118 million as of December 31, 2025 and 2024, respectively. Affiliate payables totaled approximately $94 million and $90 million as of December 31, 2025 and 2024, respectively.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt;text-indent:18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Ameren&#8217;s subsidiaries have the ability to invest excess funds or borrow funds as needed from Ameren&#8217;s money pools. Separate money pools are maintained for utility and non-state regulated entities. Excess funds that are not borrowed by other subsidiaries are invested externally. The Company administers the utility money pool and tracks internal and external funds separately. Affiliate notes receivable were approximately $117 million and $106 million as of December 31, 2025 and 2024, respectively. Affiliate notes payable were approximately $177 million and $145 million as of December 31, 2025 and 2024, respectively. The rate of interest depends on the composition of internal and external funds in the money pools. The average interest rate for borrowing for the utility money pool was 4.39% and 5.19% during the years ended December 31, 2025 and 2024, respectively. The average interest rate for borrowing for the non-state-regulated subsidiaries was 4.46% and 5.30% during the years ended December 31, 2025 and 2024, respectively.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;NOTE 5 &#8211; Retirement Benefits&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt;text-indent:18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The primary objective of the Ameren pension and postretirement benefit plans is to provide eligible employees with pension and postretirement health care and life insurance benefits. Ameren has defined benefit pension and postretirement benefit plans covering substantially all of its union employees. Ameren has defined benefit pension plans covering substantially all of its non-union employees and postretirement benefit plans covering non-union employees hired before October 2015 and union employees hired before January 2020. Ameren uses a measurement date of December 31 for its pension and postretirement benefit plans. The Company participates in Ameren's single-employer pension and other postretirement plans. Ameren's qualified pension plan is the Ameren Retirement Plan. Ameren also has an unfunded nonqualified pension plan, the Ameren Supplemental Retirement Plan, which is available to provide certain management employees and retirees with a supplemental benefit when their qualified pension plan benefits are capped in compliance with Internal Revenue Code limitations. Ameren's other postretirement plan is the Ameren Retiree Welfare Benefit Plan. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt;text-indent:18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The Company, along with other subsidiaries of Ameren, is a participant in the Ameren plans and is responsible for its proportional share of the costs. The Company's share of the pension income for 2025 and 2024 was approximately $7&#160;million and $22&#160;million, respectively. The Company's share of the post retirement benefit income for 2025 and 2024 was $10&#160;million and $10&#160;million, respectively.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfImportantDisclosuresRegardingTheFinancialStatementsTextBlock>
  <ferc:OrganizationChart id="f-2" contextRef="c-1">AmerenServicesCompanyOrgChartasof12-31-2025.pdf</ferc:OrganizationChart>
  <ferc:MethodsOfAllocationTextBlock id="f-3" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:700;line-height:112%"&gt;DESCRIPTION OF ALLOCATION FACTORS&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Service Company or AMS - Ameren Services Company&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;The following allocation factors will be utilized:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Direct&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; In addition to the allocation factors listed below, appropriate direct allocations will be made for costs benefiting a single Client Company or Other Client Company. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Allocated Direct&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; Costs applicable to two or more Client Companies will be allocated among the Client Companies based on allocation factors listed below. These factors will be assigned to a Service Request project based on the nature of the activity being performed by Service Company. Allocated Direct allocation factor assignment will reflect the cost-causation nature of the costs.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Indirect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; Functional and Corporate Indirect allocations will also be made to all affiliates. Indirect Costs shall include those costs of a general overhead basis which cannot be identified to a single Client Company or group of Client Companies. These indirect costs are defined as either functional or corporate in nature. Functional indirect costs, such as office supplies and secretarial labor, will be accumulated by functional area and distributed to Client Companies based on the ratio of total direct and direct allocated costs charged to the Client Company by a particular functional area as compared to all such costs charged to all Client Companies and Other Client Companies. Indirect costs identified as corporate in nature, such as the Service Company&#8217;s banking activities and rent, will be distributed to Client Companies based on the ratio of total direct and direct allocated costs charged to the Client Company by Service Company as compared to all such costs charged to all Client Companies and Other Client Companies.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:700;line-height:112%;text-decoration:underline"&gt;Composite Allocated Direct Factors: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Allocation Factor: 001A Operational Composite-Sales/Customers/Employees&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Based on an equal weighting of the Sales (kwh &amp;amp; dekatherm), Number of Customers (total), and/or Number of Employees (total) allocation factors. The numerator of which is the simple average of the above three factors for a Client Company and the denominator of which is for all Client Companies. This ratio will be determined annually and/or at such time as may be required due to a significant change in circumstances.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Allocation Factor: 001J Corporate Composite -Revenues/Assets/Labor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Based on an equal weighting of the Revenues (total), Assets (total), and Labor (total) allocation factors. The numerator of which is the simple average of the above three factors for a Client Company and the denominator of which is for all Client Companies. This ratio will be determined annually and/or at such time as may be required due to a significant change in circumstances.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:700;line-height:112%;text-decoration:underline"&gt;Revenue Related Allocated Direct Factors:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Allocation Factor: 002A, 002C, 002D, 002K, 002L, 002Q Number of Customers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Based on the number of customers (electric and/or gas or combination) at the end of the most recent calendar year. The numerator of which is for a Client Company and the denominator of which is for all Client Companies or a subset of Client Companies. This ratio will be determined annually, and/or at such time as may be required due to a significant change in circumstances.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Allocation Factor: 003B KWH Sales&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Based on the sales kwh volume for the most recent calendar year. The numerator of which is for a Client Company and the denominator of which is for all Client Companies. This ratio will be determined annually, and/or at such time as may be required due to a significant change in circumstances.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Allocation Factor: 006B Revenues&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%"&gt;Based on electric revenues for the most recent calendar year. The numerator of which is for a Client Company or an affected affiliate company. The denominator of which is for all Client Companies and/or affected affiliate companies. This ratio will be determined annually, or at such time as may be required due to a significant change in circumstances.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Allocation Factor: 010A Peak Load (electric)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Based on the average 12 month coincidental peak (CP) for the 12 months ending June of the prior year. The numerator of which is for a Client Company and the denominator of which is for all Client Companies. This ratio will be determined annually, and/or at such time as may be required due to a significant change in circumstances.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:700;line-height:112%;text-decoration:underline"&gt;Labor/ Employee Related Allocated Direct Factors:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Allocation Factor: 004A, 004B, 004P Number of Employees&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Based on the number of employees (contract and/or non-contract, or electric operating and/or gas operating) at the end of the most recent calendar year. The numerator of which is for a Client Company or an affected affiliate company. The denominator of which is for all Client Companies and affected affiliate companies. This ratio will be determined annually, and/or at such time as may be required due to a significant change in circumstances.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Allocation Factor: 005D Labor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Based on the Labor for the most recent calendar year. Labor includes salaries and other compensation but does not include benefits. The numerator of which is for a Client Company or an affected affiliate and the denominator of which is for all Client Companies and affected affiliate companies. This ratio will be determined annually, and/or at such time as may be required due to a significant change in circumstances. On a quarterly basis, any material unallocated AMS benefits were allocated to AIC and UEC.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:700;line-height:112%;text-decoration:underline"&gt;Asset Related Allocated Direct Factors:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Allocation Factor: 007A Total Capitalization&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Based on total capitalization (total common stockholders' equity, preferred stock, and long term debt) at the end of the most recent calendar year. The numerator of which is for a Client Company or an affected affiliate company. The denominator of which is for all Client Companies and affected affiliate companies. This ratio will be determined annually, and/or at such time as may be required due to a significant change in circumstances.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Allocation Factor: 008A Total Assets&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Based on total assets at the end of the most recent calendar year. The numerator of which is for a Client Company or an affected affiliate company. The denominator of which is for all Client Companies and affected affiliate companies. This ratio will be determined annually, and/or at such time as may be required due to a significant change in circumstances.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Allocation Factor: 008C Gross Plant-in-Service plus CWIP (Absolute Value)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Based on the Gross Plant-in Service (Absolute Value) (Total Property and Plant in Service, adding back Depreciation and Amortization, plus CWIP, adding back Nuclear Fuel Settlement) at the end of the most recent calendar year. The numerator of which is the total of Gross Plant-in-Service plus CWIP of a Client Company or affiliate company, the denominator of which is for all Client Companies or affiliates. This ratio will be determined annually, and/or at such time as may be required due to a significant change in circumstances.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Allocation Factor: U-### Undivided Interest&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Based on the fractional ownership of an asset, a pre-determined allocation will be calculated. Undivided Interest allocation allows AMS to charge costs to the project per a pre-determined ratio that remains constant over the term of the project. This ratio will be determined when the project is authorized and calculated per terms of the agreement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:700;line-height:112%;text-decoration:underline"&gt;Expenditure Related Allocated Direct Factors:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Allocation Factor: 009A Construction Expenditures&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Based on construction expenditures for the most recent calendar year. The numerator of which is for a Client Company or an affected affiliate company. The denominator of which is for all Client Companies and affected affiliate companies. This ratio will be determined annually, and/or at such time as may be required due to a significant change in circumstances.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Allocation Factor: 009B Forecasted Capital Expenditures&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Based on the 3-year total forecast for capital expenditures, as included in Ameren's most recent board-approved capital expenditure budget. The numerator is the Client Company's capital expenditure forecast and the denominator is the total capital expenditure forecast for all Client Companies. This factor will be updated annually to reflect expenditures included in the most recent board-approved capital expenditure budget. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Allocation Factor: 009C Forecasted Transmission Capital Expenditures&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Based on the 3-year total forecast for transmission capital expenditures, as included in Ameren's most recent board-approved capital expenditure budget. The numerator is the Client Company's transmission capital expenditure forecast and the denominator is the total transmission capital expenditure forecast for all Client Companies. This factor will be updated annually to reflect expenditures included in the most recent board-approved capital expenditure budget.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Allocation Factor: 018D Non-Fuel Expenditures&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Based on the dollar expenditure of non-fuel transactions. The numerator is the dollar expenditure of non-fuel transactions for a Client Company or an affected affiliate company. The denominator of which is the total dollar expenditure of non-fuel transactions, excluding AMS, for all Client Companies and affected affiliate companies. The ratio will be determined annually, and/or at such times as may be required due to a significant change in circumstances.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Allocation Factor: 015A Current Tax Expense&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Based on taxes charged (income and other) for the most recent calendar year. The numerator of which is for a Client Company or an affected affiliate company. The denominator of which is for all Client Companies and affected affiliate companies. This ratio will be determined annually, and/or at such time as may be required due to a significant change in circumstances.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Allocation Factor: 019A Governmental Affairs&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Based on the information by Ameren&#8217;s Governmental Affairs organizations as to which Client Companies and/ or Other Client Companies will be supported in the coming year. The ratio will be determined annually, and/or at such times as may be required due to a significant change in circumstances.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:700;line-height:112%;text-decoration:underline"&gt;Units &amp;amp; Usage Related Allocated Direct Factors:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Allocation Factor: 012D Electric Net Generation (Megawatt Hours)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Based on the electric net generation (megawatt hours) at the end of the most recent calendar year. The numerator of which is for a Client Company. The denominator of which is for all Client Companies. This ratio will be determined annually and/or at such time as may be required due to a significant change in circumstances.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Allocation Factor: 016A Number of Vehicles&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Based on number of vehicles at the end of the most recent calendar year. The numerator of which is for a Client Company and the denominator of which is for all Client Companies. This ratio will be determined annually, and/or at such time as may be required due to a significant change in circumstances.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Allocation Factor: 017A Number of General Ledger Transactions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Based on the number of general ledger transactions. The numerator of which is the number of general ledger transactions for a Client Company or an affected affiliate company. The denominator of which is the total number of general ledger transactions, excluding Ameren Services (AMS) and elimination corporations (ELMS), for all Client Companies and affected affiliate companies. This ratio will be determined annually, and/or at such time as may be required due to a significant change in circumstances.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Allocation Factor: 017B Number of Accounts Payable Vouchers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Based on the number of accounts payable vouchers. The numerator is the number of accounts payable vouchers for a Client Company or an affected affiliate company. The denominator of which is the total number of accounts payable vouchers, excluding AMS, for all Client Companies and affected affiliate companies. The ratio will be determined annually, and/or at such times as may be required due to a significant change in circumstances.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Allocation Factor: 017C Number of Active Projects&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Based on the number of active projects in the system. The numerator is the number of projects for a Client Company or an affected affiliate company. The denominator of which is the total number of all active projects, excluding AMS, for all Client Companies and affected affiliate companies. This ratio will be calculated annually, and/or at such time as it may be required due to a significant change in circumstances.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Allocation Factor: 017E Number of Major Projects&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Based on the number of projects greater than $25 million. The numerator is the number of projects greater than $25 million for a Client Company or an affected affiliate company. The denominator of which is the total number of projects greater than $25 million, excluding AMS, for all Client Companies and affected affiliate companies. The ratio will be determined annually, and/or at such times as may be required due to a significant change in circumstances.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Allocation Factor: 018A Number of Managed PCs&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Based on the number of computer devices managed by Information Technology. The numerator is the number of Information Technology managed PCs for a Client Company or an affected affiliate company. The denominator is the total number of managed computer devices, excluding AMS, for all Client Companies and affected affiliate companies. This ratio will be calculated annually, and/or at such time as it may be required due to a significant change in circumstances.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Allocation Factor: 018E Computer Server Usage &#8211; Other than UNIX&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Based on the number of computer non-UNIX servers assigned to a Client Company or business segment, a ratio will be determined. The business segment will be reallocated based on the appropriate factor to support multiple corporations. For example, non-UNIX computer servers that support Energy Delivery will use customer counts to reallocate. The number of non-UNIX computer servers assigned to a Client Company will be used as the numerator. The denominator will be the total number of non-UNIX computer servers assigned. The ratio will be determined annually, and/or at such times as may be required due to a significant change in circumstances.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Allocation Factor: 018F Computer Server Usage - UNIX &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Based on the number of UNIX computer servers assigned to a Client Company or business segment, a ratio will be determined. The business segment will be reallocated based on the appropriate factor to support multiple corporations. For example, UNIX computer servers that support Energy Delivery will use customer counts to reallocate. The number of UNIX computer servers assigned to a Client Company will be used as the numerator. The denominator will be the total number of UNIX computer servers assigned. The ratio will be determined annually, and/or at such times as may be required due to a significant change in circumstances.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Allocation Factor: 018G Computer Storage Device Usage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Based on the storage device usage by a Client Company or business segment, a ratio will be determined. The business segment will be reallocated based on the appropriate factor to support multiple corporations. For example, computer storage device usage that supports Energy Delivery will use customer counts to reallocate. The storage device usage assigned to a Client Company will be used as the numerator. The denominator will be the total device usage assigned. The ratio will be determined annually, and /or at such times as may be required due to a significant change in circumstances.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Allocation Factor: 020A Transmission Circuit Miles&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Based on the number of transmission circuit miles in service at the end of the most recent calendar year. For a Client Company receiving charges under this factor, the numerator is the number of in-service transmission circuit miles owned by the Client Company and the denominator is the total number of in-service transmission circuit miles owned by all Client Companies. This ratio will be determined annually, and/or at such time as may be required due to a significant change in circumstances.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Allocation Factor: 020B Number of MISO Transmission Companies&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Based on the number of companies that are Transmission Owners in MISO. For a Client Company that is a Transmission Owner in MISO, the numerator is 1 and the denominator is the total number of Ameren affiliates that are Transmission Owners in MISO. For a Client Company that is not a Transmission Owner in MISO, the factor is zero. This factor will be updated at such time that there is a change in the number of companies that are Transmission Owners in MISO.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Allocation Factor: 020D Number of Transmission Substations in Service&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Based on the number of transmission substations in service at the end of the most recent calendar year. For a Client Company receiving charges under this factor, the numerator is the number of in-service transmission substations owned by the Client Company and the denominator is the total number of in-service transmission substations owned by all Client Companies. This ratio will be determined annually, and/or at such time as may be required due to a significant change in circumstances.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:MethodsOfAllocationTextBlock>
